  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Solution of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of non-electrolyte (A) prepared by dissolving it in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> of water exerts the same osmotic pressure as that of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>05</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> glucose solution at the same temperature. The empirical formula of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The molecular mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>________g</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;(Nearest integer)</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "240",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The pressure which applied externally in the solution side to prevent the osmosis process is known as osmotic pressure. It can be denoted by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></math>.</p><p>Since,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mo>)</mo><mrow><mi>non</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>electrolyte</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mo>)</mo><mi>glucose</mi></msub></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>RT</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>RT</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>Empirical&nbsp;mass of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>12</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>05</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>05</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>240</mn></math></p>",
